TY  - RPRT
AU  - Aktuğ, Emrehan
AU  - Torul, Orhan
TI  - Political Capital: Real-Time Electoral Probabilities and the Value of Corporate Political Alignment
PY  - 2026
UR  - https://orhantorul.com/research/polcap/
KW  - Election Prediction Markets
KW  - Corporate Political Alignment
KW  - High-Frequency Returns
KW  - Political Risk
AB  - We trace partisan equity repricing during the 2024 U.S. presidential campaign using electoral probabilities and contribution records for 71 firms. A one-percentage-point increase in Trump’s winning probability is associated with a Republican-minus-Democrat return differential of about 0.04% within 150 trading minutes. The intraday differential survives alternative probability sources, sector-by-time controls, and within-sector placebo reassignments, and it mainly reflects electoral news that arrives while markets are closed. Minute-level prices show most of the July 13 event-day gap forming after the open. Longer-horizon daily evidence is less conclusive. The estimates do not establish a causal return to political giving.
ER  - 
